WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:06.940
Episode 12       What Was Normal Again?

00:12.310 --> 00:13.450
Yoka-chan!

00:13.450 --> 00:14.130
What?

00:14.130 --> 00:14.870
Over there!

00:14.870 --> 00:17.130
Yoka-chan's on that train!

00:17.770 --> 00:18.870
Shizuru-chan!

00:18.870 --> 00:20.630
He's taking Yoka-chan away!

00:36.970 --> 00:41.300
Looks like Pontaro wants to keep Yoka-chan 
within arm's reach by any means.

00:41.300 --> 00:43.260
Is she the key to 7G?

00:43.260 --> 00:44.920
I see! That's why...

00:44.920 --> 00:46.280
We need to get Yoka back!

00:48.730 --> 00:51.570
It'd be one thing if she chose to go with him,

00:51.570 --> 00:53.890
but if he took her against her will, 
then that's no good!

00:54.330 --> 00:55.120
Yeah.

01:00.210 --> 01:01.570
Don't let them escape!

01:01.570 --> 01:03.910
Or else we're all egg custard!

01:04.950 --> 01:06.810
Oh, Makoto-sensei.

01:06.810 --> 01:07.460
Heya!

01:07.460 --> 01:09.210
Pontaro got away?

01:10.400 --> 01:11.370
What about the button?!

01:11.370 --> 01:15.180
It was hidden away in a fishy place, 
but pushing it didn't do anything.

01:15.180 --> 01:17.180
<i>No! If you're going after him, 
take it with you!</i>

01:17.180 --> 01:19.780
Yoka-chan's more important right now!

01:19.780 --> 01:21.610
It'd be a pain to go back for it.

01:20.780 --> 01:22.790
<i>What's your goal here?</i>

01:22.790 --> 01:24.470
Bringing Yoka-chan back?

01:24.470 --> 01:24.990
Yeah!

01:24.990 --> 01:27.160
And turning the world back to normal?

01:27.160 --> 01:28.810
That's a part of it too, I guess.

01:28.810 --> 01:31.750
Pontaro's not as smart as he thinks he is.

01:31.750 --> 01:33.240
His actions are simple.

01:33.240 --> 01:34.830
He hid the button because it's important.

01:34.830 --> 01:35.420
End of story.

01:35.420 --> 01:36.210
What's more,

01:36.210 --> 01:40.050
he was forced to run away without 
that all-important button.

01:41.720 --> 01:43.910
<i>Ugh, why am I...</i>

01:43.910 --> 01:44.700
Princess!

01:44.700 --> 01:45.740
Princess, Princess!

01:45.740 --> 01:47.410
There's no need to worry!

01:47.410 --> 01:48.990
You're in safe hands with me.

01:49.360 --> 01:51.570
Worry? About what?

01:53.220 --> 01:55.090
You know, those scoundrels!

01:55.090 --> 01:56.070
Scoundrels...

01:56.070 --> 01:56.940
Yes, yes!

01:56.940 --> 01:59.490
They posed a threat to your safety!

01:59.490 --> 02:01.100
But please rest assured.

02:01.100 --> 02:04.600
I, Pontaro, will wholeheartedly 
exert my utmost efforts!

02:04.600 --> 02:07.340
Now then, I'm off to assess the situation!

02:07.340 --> 02:10.370
Please feel free to carry on 
as normal, Princess!

02:10.860 --> 02:12.720
As normal...

02:12.720 --> 02:14.560
What was normal again?

02:14.990 --> 02:18.680
Sleeping, waking up, eating, studying...

02:18.680 --> 02:21.610
And then... there was someone...

02:23.600 --> 02:25.030
What was that?!

02:25.480 --> 02:26.480
Pochi!

02:26.480 --> 02:27.990
Come here! Are you gone?

02:28.390 --> 02:31.100
So that button was significant, too?

02:31.100 --> 02:32.020
Significant...

02:32.020 --> 02:34.380
Is it some kind of special button?

02:34.380 --> 02:37.350
Other than just activating 7G...

02:37.880 --> 02:40.930
Maybe we need both Yoka and the button?

02:41.610 --> 02:43.150
I see, they form a set!

02:43.150 --> 02:43.960
What's that mean?

02:43.960 --> 02:48.060
It's probably related to why they 
call her the Witch of Ikebukuro.

02:48.060 --> 02:50.680
In other words, Yoka-chan 
pressed the button,

02:50.680 --> 02:53.110
the button gave Yoka-chan her powers,

02:53.110 --> 02:54.640
and then it changed the world?

02:54.640 --> 02:56.010
Oh, you're so smart!

02:56.010 --> 02:57.170
That must be it.

02:57.170 --> 02:58.080
<i>That's right!</i>

02:58.080 --> 03:00.380
It needs to be the same person 
who pushes the butto—

03:02.240 --> 03:04.320
Nakatomi Yoka pressed the button,

03:04.320 --> 03:06.360
so you need to have her press it again.

03:06.360 --> 03:10.900
I suspect that's the only way to turn both 
the world and Nakatomi Yoka back to normal.

03:18.650 --> 03:20.050
Impressive.

03:34.360 --> 03:35.570
There's two paths!

03:35.570 --> 03:37.660
Um, which way do we go again?

03:37.660 --> 03:39.300
Um, um...

03:39.300 --> 03:40.080
What?

03:40.790 --> 03:42.530
You know the way, Pochi-san?

03:42.530 --> 03:43.650
Way to go, Pochi-san!

03:50.900 --> 03:53.740
She's been acting up a lot lately.

03:53.740 --> 03:57.460
I need her to be a good 
little puppet, or else...

04:08.910 --> 04:09.550
Damn it!

04:09.550 --> 04:11.230
They sure are stubborn!

04:11.230 --> 04:12.580
It's me. Where are you?!

04:12.580 --> 04:13.530
Get your butts over here!

04:14.240 --> 04:15.220
Yoka...

04:15.220 --> 04:16.520
Shizuru-chan, this isn't good!

04:59.620 --> 05:02.180
Yoka!

05:01.120 --> 05:03.250
Yoka-chan!

05:03.250 --> 05:05.910
Yoka!

05:04.630 --> 05:07.430
It's no good! She can't hear us!

05:09.690 --> 05:11.350
You pesky brats!

05:11.350 --> 05:14.070
I won't let you have the princess!

05:20.000 --> 05:21.030
Huh? What?

05:56.300 --> 05:57.320
My mind is set!

05:57.320 --> 05:57.830
What?

05:57.830 --> 05:59.170
I'm getting on that train!

05:59.170 --> 05:59.630
No way!

05:59.630 --> 06:01.450
B-B-But how, exactly?!

06:01.450 --> 06:02.300
I'll join you!

06:02.300 --> 06:02.880
What?

06:02.880 --> 06:03.770
Me too, then.

06:03.770 --> 06:04.240
What?!

06:05.130 --> 06:06.140
Um...

06:10.560 --> 06:11.750
Damn it!

06:11.750 --> 06:15.500
If by some chance it all goes back to normal, 
I'll be the one held accountable for 7G!

06:15.500 --> 06:18.150
No way in hell I'm letting that happen!

06:18.150 --> 06:19.470
Took you long enough!

06:19.470 --> 06:21.620
You destroyed my kingdom!

06:21.620 --> 06:23.760
You'll pay the price!

06:27.060 --> 06:28.110
Out of the way!

06:30.450 --> 06:32.840
I'll turn you into skeletons!

06:33.160 --> 06:34.310
Get lost!

06:37.700 --> 06:39.420
Absolutely useless!

07:02.480 --> 07:03.260
Watch it!

07:03.260 --> 07:04.630
You could kill someone with that!

07:04.630 --> 07:05.400
You moron!

07:05.400 --> 07:06.750
I <i>want</i> all of you dead!

07:06.750 --> 07:07.390
What?

07:07.390 --> 07:08.780
You're going to kill us?

07:08.780 --> 07:09.530
That's right.

07:09.530 --> 07:13.130
You're nothing but bad news for the princess.
Ikebukuro and the princess need each other!

07:13.130 --> 07:16.650
There's no Ikebukuro without the princess! 
And there's no princess without Ikebukuro!

07:17.350 --> 07:18.590
Damn you!

07:26.590 --> 07:27.650
It's you...

07:27.650 --> 07:28.470
Okay!

07:28.470 --> 07:30.810
Beat the living daylights out of them!

07:32.430 --> 07:34.090
One question.

07:34.090 --> 07:37.730
What did you mean by 
"there's no princess without Ikebukuro"?

07:38.710 --> 07:39.900
Explain.

07:39.900 --> 07:42.720
At the core of 7G energy is Ikebukuro,

07:42.720 --> 07:45.110
with the princess as the core 
that generates it.

07:45.110 --> 07:47.070
The two of them depend on each other.

07:47.070 --> 07:50.410
The princess keeps Ikebukuro alive, 
and Ikebukuro keeps her alive.

07:50.410 --> 07:51.400
What?

07:50.410 --> 07:52.030
Huh? What? Huh?

07:51.400 --> 07:52.030
Shh!

07:52.030 --> 07:54.450
While eating away at Yoka-sama's life?

07:54.450 --> 07:55.200
Eating away?!

07:55.200 --> 07:56.070
What do you mean?

07:56.070 --> 07:57.860
Everyone dies eventually.

07:57.860 --> 08:01.050
What's wrong with the noble task 
of preserving Ikebukuro?!

08:01.050 --> 08:03.930
And is that what Yoka-sama wants?

08:03.930 --> 08:05.830
I think you've got the wrong idea.

08:05.830 --> 08:07.620
You're nothing more than a bodyguard.

08:07.620 --> 08:10.260
The one I serve is Yoka-sama.

08:10.260 --> 08:12.160
I'm not <i>your</i> bodyguard.

08:12.160 --> 08:13.010
What was that?!

08:13.010 --> 08:16.460
Is it not 7G that is the cause 
of Yoka-sama's suffering?

08:16.460 --> 08:17.790
And what if it is?!

08:17.790 --> 08:20.680
If we stop 7G, will her suffering end?

08:20.680 --> 08:21.650
I see now.

08:21.650 --> 08:23.990
7G created Yoka-chan the Witch Queen,

08:23.990 --> 08:26.220
and Yoka-chan created the world of 7G.

08:26.220 --> 08:26.720
The button!

08:26.720 --> 08:27.430
I get it.

08:27.430 --> 08:28.310
If she presses it...

08:34.630 --> 08:35.880
You stupid crow!

08:37.540 --> 08:38.690
Why are you...

08:38.690 --> 08:40.460
Yoka-sama is in your hands.

08:42.190 --> 08:44.020
He's not our enemy?

08:45.220 --> 08:47.890
When it comes to Yoka, you're on our side.

08:47.890 --> 08:49.460
Is that right?

08:49.460 --> 08:50.130
Yeah.

09:02.650 --> 09:04.140
Yoka-sama.

09:04.140 --> 09:04.940
Pochi.

09:04.940 --> 09:06.260
Please have some tea.

09:06.260 --> 09:07.510
Thanks.

09:19.340 --> 09:21.070
Will they be okay?

09:21.070 --> 09:21.920
I think so.

09:22.230 --> 09:24.670
I'm sure Yoka-chan will understand.

09:24.670 --> 09:28.700
If she doesn't, I'm sure once 
she sees this <i>NeriAli</i> book...

09:27.120 --> 09:28.710
<b>Alice in Nerima Land
Official Fanbook</b>

09:28.700 --> 09:31.470
Maybe if she reads a little ShibuTatsu...

09:31.800 --> 09:33.200
Nadeko-chan, that's...

09:33.200 --> 09:34.710
Oh, it's sweet myrtle.

09:34.710 --> 09:36.650
It's got nothing to do 
with Yoka-chan, right?

09:36.650 --> 09:37.500
You're right.

09:37.500 --> 09:38.430
Why'd I bring it?

09:40.590 --> 09:41.680
Oh, yeah.

09:41.680 --> 09:44.190
Yoka-chan said the flowers 
remind her of stars.

09:44.190 --> 09:45.300
What?

09:45.300 --> 09:46.060
When?

09:46.060 --> 09:48.450
Ages ago, in the school garden.

09:48.450 --> 09:49.440
Huh...

09:49.440 --> 09:53.180
Yoka-chan was already thinking 
about the stars back then?

09:53.720 --> 09:55.460
Yoka, recognize me?

09:55.460 --> 09:57.030
It's me, Shizuru.

09:57.440 --> 09:59.150
Shizuru...

09:59.150 --> 10:00.330
Did you forget?

10:00.330 --> 10:01.680
You don't remember me?

10:02.250 --> 10:03.300
You know...

10:03.300 --> 10:06.370
I'm not here to ask for your forgiveness.

10:06.370 --> 10:07.660
At worst...

10:07.660 --> 10:09.140
Maybe "at worst" isn't right.

10:09.140 --> 10:10.690
But you don't have to forgive me.

10:10.690 --> 10:14.400
I just wanted to apologize for hurting you!

10:14.400 --> 10:15.000
Sorry!

10:15.910 --> 10:18.830
Shizuru-chan's never been good with words.

10:18.830 --> 10:20.560
I feel embarrassed just listening!

10:20.560 --> 10:22.370
That wasn't how I really felt!

10:22.840 --> 10:24.640
Well, no, I did feel that way a little.

10:24.640 --> 10:26.880
You know how stupid I am, right?

10:26.880 --> 10:29.490
So it felt like you were 
so much better than me.

10:29.490 --> 10:33.300
And the better you were, 
the more worthless I felt.

10:33.300 --> 10:35.800
That's why I was so nasty to you.

10:35.800 --> 10:37.330
But by doing that...

10:37.820 --> 10:40.720
I was only lowering myself more.

10:40.720 --> 10:42.280
I get that now!

10:54.750 --> 10:55.640
Shizuru-chan!

10:55.640 --> 10:56.970
It's totally fine.

10:56.970 --> 10:58.800
Yoka's right to be mad at me.

10:58.800 --> 11:00.030
Yoka-chan!

11:04.440 --> 11:05.840
Stop it, Yoka-chan!

11:05.840 --> 11:08.730
Hey, why would you hit Shizuru-chan?

11:08.730 --> 11:10.640
I don't get it, Yoka-chan!

11:14.370 --> 11:15.990
No... What's going on?

11:16.280 --> 11:17.300
Yoka?

11:17.760 --> 11:20.390
Do... Do you remember now?

11:22.350 --> 11:24.710
"Like, you gotta know 
you've got no chance, right?"

11:25.090 --> 11:27.700
"You're just embarrassing yourself 
with such high hopes."

11:28.060 --> 11:31.370
"I don't care about you anymore, Yoka!"

11:32.280 --> 11:34.720
Hey, stop that, Yoka-chan!

11:34.720 --> 11:35.530
That's scary!

11:35.530 --> 11:36.510
Why?

11:37.480 --> 11:38.850
You said it.

11:38.850 --> 11:40.000
I did.

11:40.000 --> 11:44.060
I said that because I didn't 
want you to go away!

11:45.210 --> 11:47.470
Now... Now I get it!

11:47.470 --> 11:48.780
I know! I really do!

11:48.780 --> 11:51.880
It was awful to put you down 
and say you couldn't do it!

11:51.880 --> 11:53.870
But back then, I didn't want you to leave,

11:53.870 --> 11:56.000
even if it meant hurting or mocking you!

11:56.390 --> 12:00.180
Is that why you came here 
to drag me back to Agano?

12:00.180 --> 12:01.150
No!

12:01.150 --> 12:03.500
I wanted to say sorry for what I said.

12:03.500 --> 12:06.030
Also, I wanted to tell you 
that I believe in your dreams.

12:06.030 --> 12:09.370
That I support you and 
I'll be cheering you on!

12:09.940 --> 12:12.490
How vain, making it all about yourself.

12:12.490 --> 12:13.110
Hey!

12:13.110 --> 12:13.900
Yoka-chan!

12:13.900 --> 12:14.810
That's uncalled-for!

12:14.810 --> 12:16.590
Yoka-chan, you're wrong about that.

12:16.590 --> 12:19.210
I agree Shizuru-chan said some mean things.

12:19.210 --> 12:23.110
But she wouldn't have spent two years 
looking for you every day out of vanity!

12:23.110 --> 12:24.870
Or come out to Ikebukuro!

12:24.870 --> 12:26.840
Yeah, it wasn't easy getting here!

12:26.840 --> 12:28.660
I never asked, and I'm not responsible.

12:28.660 --> 12:30.380
That's right, you didn't ask us to!

12:30.380 --> 12:33.610
But if you continue to cut us off, 
nothing will change!

12:33.610 --> 12:34.840
Nothing will change...

12:34.840 --> 12:38.630
I used to think it'd be fine 
if nothing ever changed.

12:38.630 --> 12:42.440
If I could stay in Agano forever, 
with you and the others.

12:42.440 --> 12:45.100
That's why, at first, 
I just wanted to have you come back.

12:45.100 --> 12:48.020
But now I know that wouldn't be any fun.

12:48.020 --> 12:51.010
It's boring when you know the future 
and what it holds.

12:51.010 --> 12:54.880
The more mysteries and uncertainty, 
the more fun it is!

12:54.880 --> 12:59.460
You see, we ran into a lot of 
trouble from Agano to Ikebukuro!

12:59.460 --> 13:01.260
But it was so much fun!

13:01.260 --> 13:03.750
I never would've realized 
if I'd stayed in Agano.

13:03.750 --> 13:06.700
But, well, now the world 
has stopped changing.

13:06.700 --> 13:08.250
It's all come to a standstill.

13:08.250 --> 13:09.410
It's worse than that!

13:09.410 --> 13:10.860
They say it's going to shrink.

13:10.860 --> 13:13.550
I want to change and bring about change!

13:13.550 --> 13:15.190
Deep down, don't you want—

13:16.630 --> 13:17.640
Yoka-chan!

13:16.970 --> 13:18.140
Stop it!

13:18.480 --> 13:20.870
Don't decide for me how I feel!

13:27.440 --> 13:28.690
Shizuru-chan!

13:31.980 --> 13:33.040
Yoka-chan.

13:33.040 --> 13:34.290
Is your life fun now?

13:41.370 --> 13:44.170
No, it's not...

13:49.040 --> 13:50.510
It's not fun.

14:11.370 --> 14:12.620
<b>Nakatomi Yoka</b>

14:17.940 --> 14:20.330
A lot happened back in Agano.

14:20.730 --> 14:23.870
Including sad things, painful things, 
and awful things.

14:23.870 --> 14:27.060
But it was those ups and 
downs that made it fun.

14:27.060 --> 14:29.460
Yoka-chan, you have a dream, don't you?

14:29.460 --> 14:31.800
As things stand, nothing will change,

14:31.800 --> 14:34.830
but if the world goes back to normal, 
your dream might come true.

14:34.830 --> 14:36.610
You can work to make it come true.

14:36.610 --> 14:38.150
The possibility is there.

14:38.150 --> 14:39.860
The possibility...

14:39.860 --> 14:40.890
Yoka.

14:40.890 --> 14:42.930
Let's set the world in motion again.

14:45.730 --> 14:46.810
But...

14:47.190 --> 14:49.370
It'll be rough if I don't make it.

14:51.430 --> 14:53.100
It'll hurt if you fail.

14:53.440 --> 14:56.200
But I'll be cheering you on, Yoka!

14:56.540 --> 14:57.110
Yeah.

14:57.110 --> 14:59.570
I'll cheer as hard as I can! 
I'll tell you to do your best!

15:00.040 --> 15:04.010
It's way better to try and have regrets 
than not do anything at all.

15:04.010 --> 15:05.550
So I'll cheer you on!

15:11.510 --> 15:12.950
That's Sirius!

15:12.950 --> 15:13.980
Sirius?

15:13.980 --> 15:16.030
The promise star...

15:19.440 --> 15:23.030
Let's promise on that big, 
twinkling promise star.

15:23.030 --> 15:24.470
Promise star?

15:24.470 --> 15:26.070
I just made up that name.

15:26.070 --> 15:28.610
I think its name is Sirius.

15:29.010 --> 15:31.720
Let's make that our name, then.

15:31.720 --> 15:32.610
Okay.

15:40.920 --> 15:43.540
I don't deserve to be cheered on.

15:43.540 --> 15:44.430
Why not?

15:44.430 --> 15:46.820
I made fun of you.

15:46.820 --> 15:49.350
For talking big but never 
amounting to anything.

15:50.050 --> 15:51.510
And you never would.

15:51.860 --> 15:56.080
You could wither away 
and rot for all I cared.

15:56.080 --> 15:57.050
I laughed at you.

15:57.050 --> 15:58.220
Cursed you out.

15:59.430 --> 16:01.030
That's no curse.

16:03.260 --> 16:04.520
It's what I want.

16:04.520 --> 16:05.480
What?

16:05.480 --> 16:09.820
I mean, whether I stay in Agano forever or end up leaving for somewhere else,

16:09.820 --> 16:13.410
I'm happy you were thinking 
about me regardless.

16:13.980 --> 16:18.000
Shizuru-chan, you really are so stupid...

16:18.310 --> 16:20.300
Hey, Yoka-chan.

16:20.300 --> 16:23.240
Wouldn't you rather be with the rest of us
instead of being all alone here?

16:23.240 --> 16:24.280
That's right.

16:24.280 --> 16:25.890
It'd definitely be more fun that way!

16:25.890 --> 16:29.140
You can think about the future 
when the time comes.

16:31.420 --> 16:32.500
Yoka.

16:51.220 --> 16:52.440
I...

16:53.220 --> 16:54.320
It'll be fine.

17:02.590 --> 17:04.530
Oh, no, you don't!

17:07.870 --> 17:08.590
Yoka-chan!

17:08.590 --> 17:09.220
Yoka!

17:14.800 --> 17:15.990
I've got you!

17:17.460 --> 17:19.510
That scared me!

17:20.000 --> 17:21.130
My word!

17:21.130 --> 17:22.420
Now, that's a surprise!

17:22.420 --> 17:23.880
If it isn't the Witch Queen!

17:23.880 --> 17:25.800
Her name's Yoka. Nakatomi Yoka.

17:28.390 --> 17:29.760
I see now!

17:32.140 --> 17:34.310
If the world goes back to normal...

17:34.660 --> 17:36.580
Even if it doesn't...

17:36.580 --> 17:37.940
We'll think about it then!

17:37.940 --> 17:39.340
Optimism!

17:39.340 --> 17:40.710
Isn't that enough?

17:59.790 --> 18:00.720
Yoka-sama...

18:22.670 --> 18:24.170
You guys...

18:26.120 --> 18:28.500
This is, um...

18:28.500 --> 18:29.030
Hey!

18:29.030 --> 18:30.960
Was Ikebukuro like this before?

18:30.130 --> 18:30.960
Yeah, that!

18:30.960 --> 18:33.420
I feel like it was, but also not really...

18:33.420 --> 18:34.790
It's the old Yoka, at least.

18:34.790 --> 18:35.400
What?

18:35.400 --> 18:36.510
Yeah, yeah.

18:36.510 --> 18:37.600
Really?

18:37.600 --> 18:40.520
Yeah, you're 100% back to the Yoka we know.

18:40.520 --> 18:41.330
Yep.

18:41.920 --> 18:44.400
It feels a little different from before.

18:44.970 --> 18:46.400
That's correct.

18:46.400 --> 18:48.840
Even if a river appears 
to flow in the same way,

18:48.840 --> 18:50.380
the water itself is different.

18:50.380 --> 18:52.870
The same goes for towns, 
people, and the world.

18:52.870 --> 18:54.720
They appear the same, but they're not.

18:54.720 --> 18:55.990
They change over time.

18:55.990 --> 18:59.190
Thanks for the tidy summary.

18:59.480 --> 19:01.400
The world can't go back to the way it was.

19:01.400 --> 19:02.890
It continues to change.

19:02.890 --> 19:03.450
Now, then!

19:05.820 --> 19:08.490
Time to see what the world has become!

19:08.490 --> 19:10.660
Until we meet again!

19:16.900 --> 19:18.300
Huh? What?

19:18.560 --> 19:20.320
Gratitude or admiration...

19:20.320 --> 19:22.010
It's one or the other. Or both.

19:22.010 --> 19:24.310
But they've all gone back to being human...

19:24.310 --> 19:25.630
Don't think of it as going back.

19:25.630 --> 19:29.270
The ex-human zombies 
turned into brand-new humans!

19:29.270 --> 19:30.170
Makes sense.

19:30.170 --> 19:32.430
Am I still your queen?

19:35.350 --> 19:37.570
Yeah, that's where you belong.

19:37.570 --> 19:38.820
Kurokin!

19:38.820 --> 19:40.370
What about you girls?

19:43.410 --> 19:44.330
Agano!

19:49.950 --> 19:51.010
Our destination's set!

19:51.010 --> 19:53.440
All aboard the Apogee!

20:00.590 --> 20:02.440
The Apogee?

20:02.440 --> 20:04.420
Shizuru-chan named it.

20:04.420 --> 20:05.620
Why...

20:07.150 --> 20:09.320
I wonder how Agano's doing.

20:09.320 --> 20:11.500
More like, what's it like now?

20:18.600 --> 20:19.680
Huh, what?

20:19.680 --> 20:20.400
What's that sound?

20:20.400 --> 20:21.350
What was it again?

20:21.350 --> 20:22.980
Oh, I know!

20:22.490 --> 20:23.660
<b>Incoming Call</b>

20:23.650 --> 20:25.010
It worked!

20:25.010 --> 20:27.670
It must be since you stopped 7G.

20:27.670 --> 20:28.170
Over here?

20:28.450 --> 20:29.140
Yeah.

20:29.140 --> 20:31.410
It's a mix of good things, 
not-so-good things,

20:31.410 --> 20:34.090
and things where it's hard to say 
either way, all at once.

20:34.500 --> 20:36.740
I can't say that it's all disappeared.

20:36.740 --> 20:39.840
There are still a few... or rather, 
a lot of residual effects.

20:39.840 --> 20:40.720
Zenjiro.

20:40.720 --> 20:42.370
Document everyone's changes.

20:41.730 --> 20:42.970
Goodness me.

20:42.970 --> 20:45.330
The great Makoto-sensei sure is demanding—

20:47.800 --> 20:48.680
Hmm.

20:48.680 --> 20:52.530
Today's anti-choo-choo mode lasted 
39 seconds longer than yesterday.

20:52.530 --> 20:53.920
Well, that's how it is here.

20:53.920 --> 20:55.440
Be careful on your way back.

20:55.440 --> 20:58.910
You might just have a harder time 
on the return trip.

21:02.310 --> 21:03.090
Look!

21:03.090 --> 21:03.740
What's that?

21:03.740 --> 21:04.810
I see something!

21:04.810 --> 21:06.560
Another train line?

21:06.560 --> 21:07.010
Huh?

21:07.010 --> 21:08.690
Could it be the Seibu Shinjuku line?

21:08.690 --> 21:10.350
So it came back?

21:10.350 --> 21:12.620
We came back, too.

21:12.880 --> 21:15.000
Is "came back" really the right phrase?

21:15.000 --> 21:17.490
What if it's a brand-new Shinjuku line 
we don't know about?

21:17.790 --> 21:21.270
We might have jumped to 
an alternate reality, too.

21:21.270 --> 21:23.270
Can we really make it back to Agano?

21:23.270 --> 21:23.960
Right?

21:23.960 --> 21:25.330
Hey, Shizuru-chan.

21:25.330 --> 21:28.020
Why did you name it the Apogee?

21:28.020 --> 21:28.660
Huh?

21:30.630 --> 21:31.300
Ah!

21:31.300 --> 21:32.450
Good question.

21:32.450 --> 21:35.090
I wouldn't have expected it 
out of Shizuru-chan.

21:35.090 --> 21:36.370
It's a technical term, too.

21:36.370 --> 21:37.050
Yeah, why?

21:37.050 --> 21:38.260
Why, why?

21:44.150 --> 21:48.710
The moon is farthest away 
from Earth at its apogee.

21:48.710 --> 21:50.820
So it can only get closer from there.
